WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.302 --> 00:00:07.872
Soon Jean Valjean was arrested in Paris. The newspapers were full of stories about this notorious convict.

2
00:00:07.873 --> 00:00:11.100
Here is part of a story from the Journal de Paris

3
00:00:11.101 --> 00:00:15.372
: This villain had succeeded in hiding from the police for many

4
00:00:15.373 --> 00:00:21.777
years. Changing his name to Madeleine, he had even managed to become mayor in one of our small cities to the

5
00:00:21.778 --> 00:00:29.610
north. He had established a very successful business, but he was finally identified and arrested, thanks to the hard work of the

6
00:00:29.611 --> 00:00:37.515
police. Unfortunately he escaped, but he was recaptured getting out of one of the small vehicles that travel between Paris and

7
00:00:37.516 --> 00:00:44.769
Montfermeil. It is said that he used his days of freedom to withdraw a large sum that he had deposited with one of our

8
00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:49.913
bankers. The amount is estimated at six hundred to seven hundred thousand

9
00:00:49.914 --> 00:00:58.586
francs. According to notes from his trial, he has hidden the money somewhere. Thus it has proven impossible for the government to seize

10
00:00:58.587 --> 00:01:06.594
it. Valjean went to trial for the robbery of the chimney sweep. He made no attempt to defend himself and was swiftly found

11
00:01:06.595 --> 00:01:11.408
guilty. Although he was condemned to death, Valjean refused to appeal his

12
00:01:11.408 --> 00:01:16.324
case. But the king decided to change his sentence to hard labor in prison for

13
00:01:16.325 --> 00:01:22.586
life. Valjean was sent to a prison ship in Toulon and became known as Number

14
00:01:22.587 --> 00:01:28.150
9430. In the following months, the factory and the city where he had been mayor rapidly

15
00:01:28.151 --> 00:01:34.555
declined. Toward the end of October in that same year, the warship Orion arrived in the port of

16
00:01:34.556 --> 00:01:40.134
Toulon. The ship had long been in bad condition and had come to the city for

17
00:01:40.135 --> 00:01:46.380
repairs. Aboard the ship, along with some sailors, were some convicts who had been sentenced to hard labor.

18
00:01:46.381 --> 00:01:51.568
The arrival of the massive warship quickly attracted a large crowd of curious onlookers.

19
00:01:51.570 --> 00:01:56.967
Each day, as the repair work continued, people came to admire the vessel.

20
00:01:56.968 --> 00:02:01.452
One morning the crowd that was gazing at the ship witnessed an accident.

21
00:02:01.453 --> 00:02:06.356
The crew was taking in the sails when one of the sailors suddenly lost his balance.

22
00:02:06.357 --> 00:02:11.031
The crowd on the wharf shouted a cry of dismay as the man began to fall.

23
00:02:11.032 --> 00:02:16.674
He managed to grasp one of the ropes, but he was suspended helplessly high above the deck.

24
00:02:16.675 --> 00:02:19.112
The sea lay far below him.

25
00:02:19.114 --> 00:02:26.270
The shock of his fall had caused the rope to swing violently, and the poor man dangled at the end of this line.

26
00:02:26.271 --> 00:02:29.928
To go to his aid was to risk your own life.

27
00:02:29.929 --> 00:02:35.624
None of the crew, who had only recently joined the service, even dared to attempt helping him.

28
00:02:35.625 --> 00:02:39.833
In the meantime the unfortunate sailor was becoming exhausted.

29
00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:44.357
Every attempt he made to climb back up only increased the swinging of the rope.

30
00:02:44.358 --> 00:02:48.833
He did not cry out, perhaps because he did not want to waste the energy.

31
00:02:48.834 --> 00:02:52.984
It was clear to the crowd that soon he would lose his grip and fall.

32
00:02:52.985 --> 00:02:59.405
Some people on the dock had already turned away because they did not want to witness this horrible scene.

33
00:02:59.406 --> 00:03:04.071
Suddenly a man shot up the rigging with the agility of a monkey.

34
00:03:04.072 --> 00:03:12.067
The man was dressed in red, which meant he was a convict, and he wore a green cap, a sign that he was a prisoner for life.

35
00:03:12.068 --> 00:03:20.480
As the convict climbed, a gust of wind blew off his cap and showed that he had white hair. This was not a young man.

36
00:03:20.481 --> 00:03:27.972
At the first cry of alarm, the convict had run to the nearest officer and asked permission to save the sailor’s life.

37
00:03:27.973 --> 00:03:35.043
No one else onboard dared to risk such a dangerous job, so the officer granted the convict permission.

38
00:03:35.044 --> 00:03:41.543
With one blow of a hammer, the convict broke the heavy chain that was attached to the iron ring around his ankle.

39
00:03:41.544 --> 00:03:48.211
Only later would the sailors remember the man's amazing strength, how easily he had broken the chain.

40
00:03:48.212 --> 00:03:54.720
Swiftly the convict climbed the mast and stood upon the yard—a wooden support for the ship’s rigging.

41
00:03:54.721 --> 00:03:58.178
He paused for a few seconds to assess the situation.

42
00:03:58.179 --> 00:04:06.686
Those seconds felt like ages to the nervous onlookers below, who were watching the wind blow the sailor at the end of the rope back and forth.

43
00:04:06.687 --> 00:04:11.859
At last the convict took a step forward, and the crowd held its breath as one.

44
00:04:11.860 --> 00:04:18.503
He ran along the yard until he reached its tip. Then he fastened a rope to the yard and let it hang down.

45
00:04:18.504 --> 00:04:25.170
What happened next terrified the crowd. The convict began to slowly climb down the rope.

46
00:04:25.171 --> 00:04:32.170
Now, instead of seeing one man dangle at that frightening height, the crowd watched two men dangle!

47
00:04:32.171 --> 00:04:40.066
Every eye was fixed upon that pair. Not a word was spoken; the same emotion furrowed every brow.

48
00:04:40.067 --> 00:04:47.891
Every person held his or her breath, as if afraid to add the smallest whisper to the wind that was swaying the sailor and the convict.

49
00:04:47.892 --> 00:04:51.462
At last the white-haired convict reached the sailor.

50
00:04:51.463 --> 00:04:57.725
One minute more and the unfortunate sailor, exhausted and despairing, would have fallen into the sea.

51
00:04:57.726 --> 00:05:02.645
The convict secured him to the rope with one hand while clinging to it with the other.

52
00:05:02.646 --> 00:05:07.982
Finally he was seen climbing to the yard and hauling the sailor after him. Once

53
00:05:07.983 --> 00:05:13.306
there, the convict held the sailor for an instant to let him recover his strength. Then

54
00:05:13.307 --> 00:05:21.878
the older man carried the poor sailor across the yard to the mast, where he left the sailor in the hands of fellow seamen. The

55
00:05:21.879 --> 00:05:28.536
crowd burst into applause. Old officers wept, and women hugged each other on the wharf. On

56
00:05:28.537 --> 00:05:35.695
all sides voices were heard exclaiming, "That convict is a hero! He must be pardoned at once!" The

57
00:05:35.696 --> 00:05:39.869
convict, however, made a point of returning immediately to work. In

58
00:05:39.870 --> 00:05:46.258
order to go more quickly, he slid down the rigging and ran along the yard of a lower sail. All

59
00:05:46.259 --> 00:05:48.712
eyes were still following him. Then

60
00:05:48.713 --> 00:05:55.274
came the moment when all the witnesses felt alarmed because they thought they saw him hesitate and stagger. What

61
00:05:55.275 --> 00:06:00.291
was wrong? Did he feel tired, or was his head swimming from the heights? Suddenly

62
00:06:00.292 --> 00:06:05.179
the crowd cried out in horror. The convict had fallen into the sea! The

63
00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:12.417
frigate Algeciras was moored close to the Orion , and the convict plunged between the two ships.

64
00:06:12.418 --> 00:06:18.377
It was feared that he would be sucked under one or the other of the ships. Four men jumped into a boat at once.

65
00:06:18.378 --> 00:06:23.496
The people cheered them on, and once again anxiety took hold of everyone.

66
00:06:23.497 --> 00:06:31.083
The man did not rise to the surface. He simply disappeared into the sea without making even a ripple.

67
00:06:31.084 --> 00:06:38.178
The water was searched for his body until nightfall, but it was all in vain. His body was never recovered.

68
00:06:38.179 --> 00:06:45.386
The next morning the Toulon newspaper reported the incident and concluded: "The convict is presumed drowned.

69
00:06:45.394 --> 00:06:52.583
This man was registered under the number 9430, and his name was Jean Valjean."

